title: 'github get_pr_files 401s spam the log 1166x/day: no dedup, no stop-paging, no health surfacing'
updated_at: "2026-09-28T01:52:02Z"
---
Observed in daemon.log: 1166x WARN "GitHub API get_pr_files AmarooHQ/amaroo#<n> page=1 returned 401" in a single day. The app/installation token for this repo was rejected (expired/revoked), yet every PR dispatch kept calling get_pr_files and logging the 401. PR file lists were silently missing from notifications all day and nothing aggregated the failure into a single actionable signal.

Code: src/github_api.ml:444 get_pr_files; the warn is at github_api.ml:482 ("returned %d"). Callers in src/github.ml:192.

Decisions (already made):
- 401/403 are permanent auth failures: stop paging immediately after an auth-status response on page 1 (do not fetch further pages for that call); continue the dispatch without file data (current degraded behavior, just without the retry storm).
- Dedup the log: at most one WARN per (repo, status) per 10-minute window, with a suppressed-count; first occurrence stays WARN.
- Surface health: keep an in-memory last-auth-failure record (repo, status, ts, count) and include a one-line "auth failing" summary in existing github status/health output IF a cheap existing surface exists (grep first); do NOT build a new command for this.
- Actual token refresh is operator action; the fix here is stop-spam + visibility, not auth itself.

Acceptance criteria:
1. Mock transport returning 401 on page 1: exactly one log line per 10-min window regardless of dispatch count (unit test with fake clock), paging stops after the 401, dispatch still completes.
2. 200-after-401 recovery works (dedup window expires, warnings resume normally).
3. Non-auth statuses (5xx, 404, 409) keep existing behavior unchanged.
4. make test green; fmt-check clean.